{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-RS}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:92ed714ab5aa9841772b3f0c06205d07b0f193992f6d991b9b2a61519a46af3f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ccbfd78fdcbfd2560ead5567018424f9dff66739bc41ac95ed62f9f6131611f", "source_text": "Any diagram as in\nDefinition <REF_0001>\nin <MATH_0001> gives rise to a diagram in <MATH_0002>\nand the output of (RS) for this diagram in <MATH_0003>\ncan be viewed as an output for <MATH_0004> as well.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c325ff3a472f9536f41f7edcf0d4457d1398f2a7a3c62fccafdb8ec1e0d4374", "unit_id": "tag:06JC:proof"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b15315ec3c2fa7b154c0d17c24b63d47f12b572ea3fa602a460510e1a685b882", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0541ab5141a353b8f590e01ebbc27fd96740f40c8ed14812b7e50525e86371bf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma is the analogue of the fact that <MATH_0001>-fibre products\nof algebraic stacks are algebraic stacks.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5de5d05f548af2c0aed0f4234f5a5963315601c365018f59e4b68bb481953773", "unit_id": "tag:06J1:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{H} \\times_\\mathcal{F} \\mathcal{G} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{G} \\ar[d]^g \\\\\n\\mathcal{H} \\ar[r]^f & \\mathcal{F}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{H} \\times_\\mathcal{F} \\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-RS-fiber-product-morphisms}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9e72b340ac8a1f5f16057143a2698bba2d9dcb8b9db831115d4e56b352d2311", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:86cb5ef2b32f8843a09bd75598d8087a8561f73fc2436b0fe62a3d4ce4c94d28", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe <MATH_0002>-fibre product of categories cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0003>. If <MATH_0004>\nall satisfy (RS), then <MATH_0005>\nsatisfies (RS).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9a18a67450d797ea2646edc5e225ce25b785cf73a0d01713c1c39e18421a8b93", "unit_id": "tag:06L4:statement"}
